<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>RFI - All the news from France, Europe, Africa and the rest of the world.</title><description>Follow any political information, cultural, sporting and live streaming on RFI. The latest information, news and events around the world.</description><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/</link><lastBuildDate>Sun, 12 Jul 2026 18:28:51 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.rfi.fr/en/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>France</category><title>Champagne, Comté and croissants in the crossfire of climate change, experts warn</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260712-champagne-comt%C3%A9-and-croissants-in-the-crossfire-of-climate-change-experts-warn</link><description>
France's June heatwave saw temperatures in Paris hit 41C, the same average as Dubai. Experts now say that, in order to adapt to climate change, the country will have difficult choices to make when it comes to its famed lifestyle. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/ee0af75e-72b4-11f1-8c42-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/nong-03.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/ee0af75e-72b4-11f1-8c42-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/nong-03.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e81df1b4-7892-11f1-8ff1-731ac46c8d47</guid><pubDate>Sun, 12 Jul 2026 15:52:34 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/ee0af75e-72b4-11f1-8c42-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/nong-03.jpg">REUTERS - Tom Nicholson</source><dc:creator>Alison Hird</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France remembers 'old demons' of antisemitism on first annual Dreyfus day</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260712-france-remembers-old-demons-of-antisemitism-on-first-annual-dreyfus-day</link><description>
Sunday saw France observe its first annual day of commemoration for Alfred Dreyfus, a Jewish army officer wrongly convicted of treason in one of the country's most notorious cases of antisemitism. With reports of hate speech on the rise, President Emmanuel Macron said France had yet to shed its "old demons" of prejudice.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e5d9c7be-7dee-11f1-b4bd-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B9Y88MK.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e5d9c7be-7dee-11f1-b4bd-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B9Y88MK.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">21a8c7dc-7d3a-11f1-84f6-9f5186b7b518</guid><pubDate>Sun, 12 Jul 2026 12:44:22 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e5d9c7be-7dee-11f1-b4bd-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B9Y88MK.jpg">© AFP - THOMAS SAMSON </source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>In Zimbabwe, community seed banks are reviving indigenous crops</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260712-in-zimbabwe-community-seed-banks-are-reviving-indigenous-crops</link><description>
Zimbabwean farmers are reviving drought-resistant traditional crops through a community seed bank, helping them cope with worsening climate variability. The initiative, rooted in indigenous knowledge, is strengthening food security and offering a safety net against future droughts and floods.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c5c81e88-7620-11f1-bb52-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Smallholder-farmers-sorting-seeds-of-small-grains-in-Chipinge-Credit-FAO.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c5c81e88-7620-11f1-bb52-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Smallholder-farmers-sorting-seeds-of-small-grains-in-Chipinge-Credit-FAO.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">83ce4e20-7621-11f1-8440-594032ce8249</guid><pubDate>Sun, 12 Jul 2026 13:57:55 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c5c81e88-7620-11f1-bb52-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Smallholder-farmers-sorting-seeds-of-small-grains-in-Chipinge-Credit-FAO.jpg">© FAO</source><dc:creator>Farai Shawn Matiashe</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>China's rising foie gras industry has France looking over its shoulder</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260712-china-s-rising-foie-gras-industry-has-france-looking-over-its-shoulder</link><description>
China has risen rapidly to become the world's second-largest producer of foie gras, but producers in France say they are not yet worried about losing their long-held dominance of one of the country's best-known delicacies.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6a231470-7166-11f1-a633-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-06-20T001111Z-1347002243-RC26YKAZ0BQ4-RTRMADP-3-CHINA-FRANCE-FOIE-GRAS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6a231470-7166-11f1-a633-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-06-20T001111Z-1347002243-RC26YKAZ0BQ4-RTRMADP-3-CHINA-FRANCE-FOIE-GRAS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4e11bada-7160-11f1-80ca-c19e380bf25d</guid><pubDate>Sun, 12 Jul 2026 09:53:18 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6a231470-7166-11f1-a633-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-06-20T001111Z-1347002243-RC26YKAZ0BQ4-RTRMADP-3-CHINA-FRANCE-FOIE-GRAS.jpg">© Reuters/Tingshu Wang</source><dc:creator>Zeenat Hansrod</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Heatwave forces Tour de France to shorten stage for first time</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260712-heatwave-forces-tour-de-france-to-shorten-stage-for-first-time</link><description>
Tour de France organisers have shortened Sunday's stage by 30km due to extreme heat, the first time in the history of the cycling race that high temperatures have forced a change to the route.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/2977ae12-7dd3-11f1-978d-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B9DV4RN.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/2977ae12-7dd3-11f1-978d-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B9DV4RN.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a5385368-7dd2-11f1-a47d-5df6a9464878</guid><pubDate>Sun, 12 Jul 2026 09:23:01 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/2977ae12-7dd3-11f1-978d-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B9DV4RN.jpg">© Loic VENANCE / AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>Argentina struggle past Switzerland to set up semi-final showdown with England</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260712-argentina-struggle-past-switzerland-to-set-up-semi-final-showdown-with-england-world-cup-2026</link><description>
Defending champions Argentina needed two goals in extra time to subdue Switzerland 3-1 on Saturday night and advance to a semi-final clash against England.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/25b9f8d4-7db5-11f1-b208-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/julian-alvarez.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/25b9f8d4-7db5-11f1-b208-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/julian-alvarez.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cb3c34ca-7db5-11f1-85b7-6bf5e1a7261e</guid><pubDate>Sun, 12 Jul 2026 05:52:48 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/25b9f8d4-7db5-11f1-b208-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/julian-alvarez.jpg">© AFP - ODD ANDERSEN </source><dc:creator>Paul Myers</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>Norway boss Solbakken rues bad luck in World Cup defeat to England</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260712-norway-boss-solbakken-rues-bad-luck-in-world-cup-defeat-to-england-world-cup-2026</link><description>
Norway head coach Stale Solbakken rued his side's bad luck with refereeing decisions during their quarter-final defeat to England on Saturday.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0547ace6-7da5-11f1-bee6-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/stale.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0547ace6-7da5-11f1-bee6-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/stale.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">77997d44-7d99-11f1-bf9e-6b0d17f98c74</guid><pubDate>Sun, 12 Jul 2026 04:56:42 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0547ace6-7da5-11f1-bee6-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/stale.jpg">© AFP - CHANDAN KHANNA </source><dc:creator>Paul Myers</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Iran strikes Gulf neighbours after new US attacks</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260711-iran-strikes-gulf-neighbours-after-new-us-attacks</link><description>
Tehran announced it was closing the Strait of Hormuz on Sunday and launched missiles and drones at its Gulf neighbours, in retaliation for new US strikes following an attack by Iranian forces on a merchant vessel that was abandoned in flames by its crew.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/05400d62-74f7-11f1-bafd-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/e7c23327786f81add837233b161f4dbce07d6ccb.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/05400d62-74f7-11f1-bafd-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/e7c23327786f81add837233b161f4dbce07d6ccb.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">dccc9e2e-7d0f-11f1-9958-51c68aff20dd</guid><pubDate>Sat, 11 Jul 2026 10:04:10 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/05400d62-74f7-11f1-bafd-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/e7c23327786f81add837233b161f4dbce07d6ccb.jpg">© - / AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>Bellingham upstages Kane and Haaland to fire England into World Cup semi-finals</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260711-bellingham-upstages-kane-and-haaland-to-fire-england-into-world-cup-semi-finals-world-cup-2026</link><description>
Jude Bellingham scored twice on Saturday as England came from behind to beat Norway 2-1 and advance to the World Cup semi-finals for the second time in three tournaments.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/73f656b6-7d77-11f1-abdf-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/jude-bellingham.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/73f656b6-7d77-11f1-abdf-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/jude-bellingham.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b40ddc2c-7d74-11f1-8f88-5713c269860a</guid><pubDate>Sat, 11 Jul 2026 23:52:31 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/73f656b6-7d77-11f1-abdf-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/jude-bellingham.jpg">© AFP - PATRICIA DE MELO MOREIRA </source><dc:creator>Paul Myers</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>As Germany cuts a deal on US missiles, Europe weighs up dependence on Washington</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260712-as-germany-cuts-a-deal-on-us-missiles-europe-weighs-up-dependence-on-washington-tomahawk</link><description>
Germany is set to buy Tomahawk missiles to plug an urgent gap in its defence, in spite of a European Union drive to lessen dependence on American weapon systems. The deal comes after a Franco-German tank maker's stock market listing stalled and a flagship European fighter jet project collapsed. Can Europe really arm itself, or is autonomy a pipe dream?
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/d35edad0-9d38-11f0-b06f-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-36PY84L.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/d35edad0-9d38-11f0-b06f-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-36PY84L.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7885640c-7c1d-11f1-aa2b-63849889c913</guid><pubDate>Sun, 12 Jul 2026 07:04:02 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/d35edad0-9d38-11f0-b06f-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-36PY84L.jpg">©  AUSTRALIAN DEFENCE / AFP</source><dc:creator>Jan van der Made</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Eiffel Tower, Louvre close early as France faces third heatwave in three months</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260711-eiffel-tower-louvre-close-early-as-france-faces-third-heatwave-in-three-months</link><description>
Three of France's biggest tourist attractions, the Eiffel Tower, the Louvre and the Musée d'Orsay, will close early all weekend as an intense heatwave grips the country for the third time since May. A red alert is in place across Paris and most of north-west France.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7827c9b6-6fd2-11f1-a33b-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-06-24T132434Z-1885014167-RC2SXLAUYP8N-RTRMADP-3-EDF-NUCLEAR.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7827c9b6-6fd2-11f1-a33b-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-06-24T132434Z-1885014167-RC2SXLAUYP8N-RTRMADP-3-EDF-NUCLEAR.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6479fc4c-7d27-11f1-8781-d94853d11127</guid><pubDate>Sat, 11 Jul 2026 13:52:43 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7827c9b6-6fd2-11f1-a33b-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-06-24T132434Z-1885014167-RC2SXLAUYP8N-RTRMADP-3-EDF-NUCLEAR.jpg">© REUTERS - Sarah Meyssonnier </source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Relations between Algeria and Mali thaw after year-long rift over drone</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260711-relations-between-algeria-and-mali-thaw-after-year-long-rift-over-drone</link><description>
Mali and Algeria have reopened their airspace to each other's planes and reinstated their ambassadors, the countries have announced, more than a year after the destruction of a Malian drone strained relations between the neighbours.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/f199ccbe-2b3a-11f0-b2e8-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000_426D8WR.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/f199ccbe-2b3a-11f0-b2e8-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000_426D8WR.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e4a74d28-7d06-11f1-b2ff-1b5a90cdefe5</guid><pubDate>Sat, 11 Jul 2026 11:12:56 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/f199ccbe-2b3a-11f0-b2e8-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000_426D8WR.jpg">© AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>French farmers race to adapt as repeated heatwaves hit crops and livestock</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260711-french-farmers-race-to-adapt-as-repeated-heatwaves-hit-crops-and-livestock</link><description>
After weeks of sweltering heat and drought, farmers and analysts fear France's maize crop could be down by a third this year – making it the smallest in 35 years. Poultry farmers are also counting their losses as many as 3 million broiler chickens died within a few days in in June. The damage is a result of three heatwaves that have already hit France this year, and is only set to intensify as climate change disrupts agriculture across Europe.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/486e780c-7b7e-11f1-a361-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-08T125055Z-1820761388-RC2N9MA2RTCP-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-FRANCE-AGRICULTURE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/486e780c-7b7e-11f1-a361-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-08T125055Z-1820761388-RC2N9MA2RTCP-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-FRANCE-AGRICULTURE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c040005c-7c6a-11f1-ab2f-113e7a8a35f2</guid><pubDate>Sat, 11 Jul 2026 07:04:10 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/486e780c-7b7e-11f1-a361-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-08T125055Z-1820761388-RC2N9MA2RTCP-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-FRANCE-AGRICULTURE.jpg">© Benoit Tessier / REUTERS</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>African results justify World Cup slots increase amid criticism</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260711-african-results-justify-world-cup-slots-increase-amid-criticism</link><description>
When four-time World Cup winners Italy failed to qualify for the 2026 tournament, then head coach Gennaro Gattuso lamented that Africa had so many places at the global showcase. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/43e3e7d2-7cfe-11f1-99d3-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/be55411e7e2fcd9ccbc5f96ed0fe432ab2e3b214.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/43e3e7d2-7cfe-11f1-99d3-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/be55411e7e2fcd9ccbc5f96ed0fe432ab2e3b214.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">44d7ced8-7cfe-11f1-afb8-a7125e438b74</guid><pubDate>Sat, 11 Jul 2026 07:58:13 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/43e3e7d2-7cfe-11f1-99d3-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/be55411e7e2fcd9ccbc5f96ed0fe432ab2e3b214.jpg">© Odd ANDERSEN / AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>EU lawmakers give digital euro the green light, but rollout still years away</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260710-eu-lawmakers-give-digital-euro-the-green-light-but-rollout-still-years-away</link><description>
EU lawmakers on Thursday backed kickstarting negotiations on creating a digital version of the euro, as the European Union races to introduce the currency. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/81fe24b6-7b9f-11f1-8af5-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-96UV6ZR.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/81fe24b6-7b9f-11f1-8af5-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-96UV6ZR.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d0862a66-7b9f-11f1-92d7-5b9af79f737d</guid><pubDate>Fri, 10 Jul 2026 19:40:04 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/81fe24b6-7b9f-11f1-8af5-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-96UV6ZR.jpg">AFP - NICOLAS TUCAT</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>Spain overcome Belgium to set up World Cup semi-final clash with France</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260710-spain-overcome-belgium-to-set-up-world-cup-semi-final-clash-with-france-world-cup-2026</link><description>
Mikel Merino scored a late winner for the second game running to send Spain into the semi-finals of the 2026 World Cup with a 2-1 victory over Belgium.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/41ecacf8-7cb7-11f1-9d87-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/mikel-merino.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/41ecacf8-7cb7-11f1-9d87-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/mikel-merino.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">155bd7d8-7c8d-11f1-9904-8d9d788b306c</guid><pubDate>Fri, 10 Jul 2026 23:37:51 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/41ecacf8-7cb7-11f1-9d87-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/mikel-merino.jpg">© AFP - ETIENNE LAURENT</source><dc:creator>Paul Myers</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Surprise alliance hands anti-independence bloc control of New Caledonia Congress</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260710-surprise-alliance-gives-non-independence-bloc-control-of-new-caledonia-congress</link><description>
The anti-independence bloc has won control of New Caledonia's deliberative assembly, after securing the backing of a small party – despite the two sides holding sharply different views on the future of the French Pacific territory.
